"""State income tax and state payroll deductions on wages for the take-home pay calculator (/tools/take-home-pay/ and one page per state).

Read 19 Nov 2026. Most states come from their own government site or statute. "secondary": the site could not be opened for this check (it blocks
automated reading), so the figures come from excerpts of the state's documents and the Tax Foundation table, and the page says so. WAITING lists
the states whose rules are still to be built or whose figures disagree (recapture, a mandatory county tax, unread limits).

b: brackets of taxable income [upper limit, rate], None for the top. d: standard deduction. e: personal exemption. c: credit taken off the tax.
base "wages": salary less pre-tax contributions; "fed": federal taxable income. pay: [name, rate, wage cap, yearly maximum].
Optional rules: std_phase and credit_phase [income where it starts, amount lost per dollar above]; add_over [taxable income, fixed tax added above it];
ex_steps [[income up to, exemption per person]]; fed_ded: the share of federal income tax that is deductible, by income, with a cap.

Run `python3 state_tax.py` to check the figures against sums worked out by hand.
"""
